---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAILS } from '../lib/site';
---

<Layout title="Delete Account">
  <Header />

  <main class="page-shell">
    <article class="prose-section">
      <p class="eyebrow">Your data, your decision</p>
      <header>
        <h1>Delete your Gurudevi account</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Request deletion here if you cannot access the app. We verify each request before changing an account or its data.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="prose-card">
        <h2>How to request deletion</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>If you can sign in, use the account deletion option in Gurudevi. This is the fastest way to associate a request with your account.</li>
          <li>
            Email us at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAILS.support}`}>{CONTACT_EMAILS.support}</a>.
          </li>
          <li>Use the subject: <span class="font-semibold">“Delete my Gurudevi account”</span>.</li>
          <li>
            Include:
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mt-2 space-y-1">
              <li>The email/phone number you used to sign in</li>
              <li>Your role (Teacher / Student / Principal)</li>
              <li>Your school name (if applicable)</li>
              <li>Any context you want us to know (optional)</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
        </ol>

        <div class="pt-2">
          <a
            class="button button--primary"
            href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAILS.support}?subject=Delete%20my%20Gurudevi%20account&body=Please%20delete%20my%20Gurudevi%20account.%0A%0AEmail%20or%20phone%20used%20to%20sign%20in%3A%20%0ARole%20(Teacher%2FStudent%2FPrincipal)%3A%20%0ASchool%20(if%20applicable)%3A%20%0A%0AAdditional%20context%20(optional)%3A%20`}
          >
            Email deletion request
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="prose-card prose-card--muted">
        <h2>What happens after a request</h2>
        <p>
          We acknowledge the request, verify that it comes from the account holder, and check whether a school, guardian, safety,
          fraud-prevention, or legal retention obligation affects the request. Once verified, the account is soft-deactivated while
          the deletion is scheduled; this stops normal access but is not presented as completed deletion.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm opacity-80">
          When deletion is completed, we delete or anonymize account-associated data unless a specific security, fraud-prevention,
          institutional recordkeeping, safeguarding, or legal obligation requires limited retention. If that applies, we will explain
          the category and basis before completion. Read the <a href="/privacy#retention-and-deletion">retention and deletion policy</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
